# HCP Terraform Stacks source-bundle exclusions
#
# Stacks source bundles include the entire VCS-tracked repo (not just the
# Stack working_directory). This file tells Terraform/HCP to exclude paths
# that are not part of the deploy. Without it, large workshop / docs / asset
# files inflate the bundle past HCP's source-bundle size limit and the
# plan errors with: "creating source bundle archive: source bundle is too large".

# Workshop authoring artifacts (Workshop Studio content + reveal-md preview build)
workshop/

# Project planning + research (GSD planning state, never deployed)
.planning/

# Source assets for the workshop (Excalidraw diagrams, brand PNGs, AWS logo)
# These produce SVGs in workshop/static/images/ which are also excluded.
assets/

# Top-level slide deck + reveal-md config
slides.md
reveal-md.json

# Documentation files (referenced from infrastructure/docs/ which IS included)
README.md
TESTING.md
LICENSE

# Repo-local AI assistant guidance
CLAUDE.md
.claude/

# Python venv if anyone runs the excalidraw-to-svg pipeline locally
.venv/

# IDE + OS noise
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
